<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Sometimes I'm faint and weary,</l><l>He knows that I am weak;</l><l>And as He bids me lean on Him,</l><l>His help I gladly seek;</l><l>He leads me in the paths of light,</l><l>Beneath a sunny sky;</l><l>And so we walk together,</l><l>My Lord and I.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>He knows how much I love Him,</l><l>And if I love Him well;</l><l>But with what love He loveth me,</l><l>My tongue can never tell;</l><l>It is an everlasting love,</l><l>Much more as days go by;</l><l>And so we love each other,</l><l>My Lord and I.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>I tell Him all my sorrows,</l><l>I tell Him all my joys;</l><l>I tell Him all that pleases me,</l><l>I tell Him what annoys;</l><l>He tells me what I ought to do,</l><l>He tells me how to try;</l><l>And so we walk together,</l><l>My Lord and I.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>He knows my heart's such longing,</l><l>Some weary soul to win;</l><l>And so He bids me go and speak,</l><l>The loving word for Him;</l><l>He bids me tell His wondrous love,</l><l>And why He came to die;</l><l>And so we work together,</l><l>My Lord and I.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
